# Line-ending policy: LF in the repository, LF on checkout.
#
# This repo is edited from both Windows and WSL and lives inside a OneDrive tree.
# Without an explicit policy, a Windows editor rewrites every line of every file
# as CRLF, so `git status` reports all 38 tracked files as modified and real
# changes are impossible to see in a diff. History is LF throughout except for a
# handful of files that were committed from a CRLF working tree; `git add
# --renormalize .` brings those back in line.
*               text=auto eol=lf

# Source and config: always text, always LF.
*.py            text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.toml          text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
*.csv           text eol=lf
*.txt           text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.cfg           text eol=lf
*.ipynb         text eol=lf

# Binary: never convert, never diff as text. NIfTI volumes and the npz cache are
# gitignored, but declare them so an accidental `git add -f` cannot corrupt them.
*.xlsx          binary
*.xls           binary
*.zip           binary
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.pdf           binary
*.pt            binary
*.pth           binary
*.npy           binary
*.npz           binary
*.nii           binary
*.nii.gz        binary
*.gz            binary
